# Security Rules

## Authentication & Authorization
- Use Keycloak OIDC for authentication
- Verify JWT tokens on every request
- Check role-based permissions before data access
- Implement session timeout and token rotation
- Never trust client-side role claims without server verification

## Input Validation
- Validate ALL inputs at system boundaries
- Use schema validation (Pydantic, Zod, etc.)
- Reject unexpected fields (strict mode)
- Limit string lengths, numeric ranges
- Sanitize file names and paths (prevent traversal)

## SQL Injection Prevention
- ALWAYS use parameterized queries or ORM
- NEVER concatenate user input into SQL strings
- Use allowlists for dynamic table/column names
- Log suspicious query patterns

## XSS Prevention
- Use framework default escaping (React JSX)
- Never use dangerouslySetInnerHTML without sanitization
- Set Content-Security-Policy headers
- Validate URLs before rendering links

## SSRF Prevention
- Validate all user-provided URLs
- Block private IP ranges (10.x, 172.16-31.x, 192.168.x)
- Use allowlists for external service URLs
- Never follow redirects to internal addresses

## Secrets Management
- Environment variables for all secrets
- Fernet encryption for secrets stored in DB
- Rotate credentials on schedule
- Never log or return secrets in API responses
